There are forgotten places in the world, places lost not just due to the shifting of time, but hidden away to seal the dangers within.

Tales that once warned us away are now folklore or have been forgotten but the hidden places still remain. That which is lost, can always be found.

The scraps of paper point to a place in the endless plains. Though now sleepy grasslands farmers there talk of plows catching long buried foundations. 

I may have found it! A weathered door of stone, set into the side of a rocky hillock. There are recent tracks here, I'm not as alone as I'd hoped.

There are bandits here, a roving band that's taken up residence for the winter. They caught me poking around and locked me up, at least they left me with my books.

I managed to escape, and even snatched some cheese on the way out. The bandits had me translating inscriptions but they've been acting more and more strangeley, they barely even sleep anymore.